1. In frontend/src/pages/profile/MedicalVault.jsx, add the Biomarker Trends section:
   a. Change the function signature to accept new prop: `{ archive, loadingArchive, expandedId, setExpandedId, pathologyReports }` — pathologyReports is the raw archive filtered to type=pathology for client-side trend computation.
   b. Inside the component, compute trends from pathologyReports (array of pathology records from archive) using client-side logic — do NOT call a new endpoint unless data is insufficient. The archive prop already has all pathology records with report_data. Group by biomarker name (lowercase key), collect {date, value} pairs sorted by created_at.
   c. Add state: `const [selectedBiomarker, setSelectedBiomarker] = useState(null);`
   d. After the existing vault list div, add a new section titled 'Biomarker Trend Timeline' (only render if pathologyReports.length > 0 and at least one biomarker has 2+ entries):
```jsx
// Compute trends from pathology records in archive
const biomarkerMap = {};
archive.filter(r => r.type === 'pathology').forEach(record => {
  let bms = [];
  try { bms = typeof record.report_data === 'string' ? JSON.parse(record.report_data) : (record.report_data || []); } catch(e){}
  const dateStr = new Date(record.created_at).toISOString().split('T')[0];
  bms.forEach(bm => {
    if (!bm.name || bm.value == null) return;
    const key = bm.name.toLowerCase().trim();
    if (!biomarkerMap[key]) biomarkerMap[key] = { display: bm.name, unit: bm.unit || '', data: [] };
    biomarkerMap[key].data.push({ date: dateStr, value: parseFloat(bm.value), source_id: record.id });
  });
});
const trendBiomarkers = Object.entries(biomarkerMap).filter(([, v]) => v.data.length >= 2).map(([k, v]) => ({ key: k, ...v }));
```
   e. Biomarker dropdown: `<select>` populated from trendBiomarkers. On change, `setSelectedBiomarker(key)`.
   f. When a biomarker is selected, show:
      - Latest value + unit (last entry by date)
      - Previous value (second-to-last)
      - Absolute change (latest - previous, formatted with sign)
      - Percentage change ((abs/previous)*100, formatted with sign)
      - Status badge using this logic: determine direction-aware biomarkers:
        * lower_is_better: glucose, hba1c, cholesterol, ldl, triglycerides, creatinine, urea, bilirubin
        * higher_is_better: hemoglobin, hdl, platelets (when low)
        * For lower_is_better: increase → 'Worsening' (red), decrease → 'Improving' (green)
        * For higher_is_better: increase → 'Improving', decrease → 'Worsening'
        * All others: change > 0.001 → 'Changed' (yellow), else → 'Stable' (gray)
      - Disclaimer: 'These trend observations are for informational purposes only and do not constitute a medical diagnosis. Please consult your doctor for interpretation.'
   g. Chart: render a pure SVG line chart (no library). SVG viewBox='0 0 400 120'. Plot dots and a polyline path. X-axis = date labels, Y-axis = value range. Use min/max of values to scale. Minimum 2 data points required. Style: stroke color var(--theme-accent), fill none, dot circles r=4 fill white.
   h. Empty state when no biomarker has 2+ records: 'No biomarker history available yet. Upload a lab report to start tracking trends.' in a muted font-monospace block.
   i. Pass the prop from Profile.jsx: in Profile.jsx, in the MedicalVault component usage (inside the vault tab), pass `pathologyReports={archive.filter(r => r.type === 'pathology')}` — archive is already computed in Profile.jsx.

